onvif-profile.patch modifies go2rtc: the ONVIF server advertises the size and
frame rate of the stream's running H.264 producer, else the ONVIF_WIDTH,
ONVIF_HEIGHT, ONVIF_FPS and ONVIF_BITRATE environment variables, else the
original 1920x1080, 30 fps, 8192 kbit/s. It also hardens the H.264 SPS decoder
against crafted values (frame rate overflow, pic order cycle, picture size),
and answers SystemReboot with a SOAP fault instead of exiting.

health-endpoint.patch modifies go2rtc: it adds a read-only GET /api/health that
reports each stream's producer and consumer states and counters, without any
URL, source or remote address, and never waits on a source being dialled.

no-api-source.patch modifies go2rtc: API queries only find streams defined in
the config; they can no longer create a stream, change a stream's source or
push a producer into a stream (WHEP included), and a WebSocket offer's own ICE
servers are ignored.

onvif-vendor-identity.patch modifies go2rtc: GetDeviceInformation and GetScopes
announce the ONVIF_NAME, ONVIF_MANUFACTURER, ONVIF_MODEL and ONVIF_LOCATION
environment variables instead of the original "go2rtc" identity (unchanged when
they are not set), with scope values URL-escaped and device fields XML-escaped.

check-secrets.sh, run before go2rtc by the image's entrypoint, is not part of
go2rtc: it exports each credential file KEY percent-encoded as KEY_URL, and
refuses one holding a character that breaks go2rtc's config text.

